The goal of this project is to build a web-based forecasting tool using the ARIMA model. It allows non-technical users to:

Upload a time series dataset (like stock prices, sales, etc.)

Configure ARIMA parameters (p, d, q)

Automatically build and apply a forecasting model

See forecast results and visualizations

Run everything through a simple browser interface

This eliminates the need for users to write Python code or understand ARIMA internals.
Streamlit is an open-source Python framework that lets you build interactive web apps directly from Python scripts — especially designed for data science and machine learning.

 Key Features:
Write a simple .py file — no HTML/CSS/JS needed.

Automatically creates a user interface from Python code.

Great for ML models, data visualization, dashboards.

Instantly shows plots, dataframes, widgets like sliders and buttons.
ngrok is a tool that lets you expose a local server to the internet. It creates a secure public URL that forwards to your local machine or environment (like Colab or Jupyter).

 Why Do We Use ngrok?
Streamlit runs on localhost:8501 (not accessible from the web).

Google Colab, where you're likely running the code, doesn’t support direct ports.

ngrok tunnels that port through the internet, giving you a public link you can click.
How ngrok Works:
You run ngrok.connect("http://localhost:8501")

ngrok generates a secure public URL (e.g., https://xyz123.ngrok.io)

Anyone with the link can access your app (hosted on your Colab).

These are the libraries imported at the top of the app:
Library	Purpose
streamlit	Builds the interactive web interface (e.g., file upload, inputs, charts).
pandas	Handles data loading, manipulation, and processing (e.g., CSV, time index).
numpy	Numerical operations (used to check data types or handle numbers).
matplotlib.pyplot	Used for plotting time series graphs directly.
ARIMA from statsmodels	Fits ARIMA models for time series forecasting.
mean_squared_error from sklearn.metrics	Calculates accuracy by comparing forecast to actual values.
warnings	Suppresses non-critical warnings to keep the output clean.
